course: dictionary
lesson: 2588
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A dent is a small hollow pressed into a hard surface, like a car door that a stone or a ball has hit. Dent can also be a verb, which means to make such a hollow: «Big hailstones can dent cars.» Here dent is an action, and the hailstones are doing it.
explain: Read the whole sentence before you decide what a word means. «Do not eat from a can that is swollen or badly dented along its seams.» A dented can has a hollow pressed into its metal, and the seams are the joins where the metal is folded together. Swap in your meaning: a can with a hollow pressed into it still makes sense.
explain: Dent also has meanings that are not about metal. «Make a dent in» means reduce something a bit, so «make a dent in your homework» means get some of it done. To dent someone's confidence means to weaken it, so the word can describe feelings too.
fact: A dent is a small hollow made in a hard surface when something hits or presses it.
fact: As a verb, dent means to make a dent in something: «Big hailstones can dent cars.»
fact: «Make a dent in» means reduce something a bit, as in «make a dent in your homework».
fact: To dent someone's confidence or pride means to harm or weaken it, so they feel less sure of themselves.
fact: In French, une dent (say DAHN) means a tooth, so it is a different word, even though it looks similar.
exercise: «The car door had a dent in it after the hailstorm.» What is a dent? | A bright, shiny coat of paint | A loud noise from the engine | *A small hollow pressed into a hard surface
exercise: «Doing the first ten sums will make a dent in your homework.» What does make a dent in mean here? | Lose all of it | *Reduce it a bit, so some of it is done | Make a hole right through it | Copy it out
exercise: «Her pride was dented when she lost the race.» Which word best matches dented here? | Washed | Painted | *Hurt or weakened | Lengthened
test: «Big hailstones can dent cars.» In this sentence, what kind of word is dent? | A noun, a thing | A question word | *A verb, an action | An adjective, describing a colour
test: «Do not eat from a can that is badly dented along its seams.» Why is this a warning? | *The can may be damaged, so the food may not be safe | Dented cans taste better | Seams are a kind of food | Dents make cans lighter, so they float
exam: In «Hailstones can dent cars», what does dent mean, and how does the sentence show it? | The colour the cars are painted | *To make a small hollow in a hard surface, shown by the hailstones hitting the cars | Something you buy from a shop | A sound made by the hail
